DiscoBSD/GBA native ARM toolchain - validation harnesses (Phase 1b + 1c).
Full status in sys/arch/gba/NOTES.toolchain sections 8-9.

The ARM assembler and linker are now INTEGRATED into the tree and built for
MACHINE_ARCH=arm:
  ../as_arm.c        -> usr.bin/as  (built as `as` for arm; as.c for mips)
  ../../ld/ld_arm.c  -> usr.bin/ld  (built as `ld` for arm; ld.c for mips)
This directory keeps the reproducible test harnesses + inputs. `build.sh`
compiles those same sources into local host binaries (asarm, ldarm, smlrc-arm)
for the harnesses.

as_arm.c - ARMv4T assembler for the exact subset usr.bin/smlrc/cgarm.c emits:
             as_arm -e "<one instr>"   -> print the 32-bit encoding (oracle)
             as_arm -o out.o in.s      -> DiscoBSD a.out relocatable object
             as_arm -b in.s out.bin    -> flat image (dev/test)
           Validated: 42/42 encodings byte-exact vs arm-none-eabi-as; 22/22
           single-object programs run in Unicorn.
ld_arm.c - ARM linker: reads a.out objects, lays out text/data/bss, resolves
           globals, applies ARM relocs (ABS32 + PC24), writes a linked image:
             ld_arm -Ttext=<hex> -e <entry> -o out.bin a.o b.o ...
           (Thumb interworking veneers: TODO, for a Thumb libc.)

FULL SELF-HOSTED CHAIN (no GNU tools): smlrc-arm -> as_arm -o -> ld_arm -> run.
Validated on cross-object calls, bss globals, division via a self-hosted
__aeabi runtime (rt.c), recursion, loops, arrays.

Build + validate:
  pip install --user --break-system-packages unicorn
  ./build.sh              # builds asarm, ldarm, smlrc-arm from the tree sources
  python3 run_ld.py       # fully self-hosted chain; or run.py / run_asarm.py

Test inputs: suite.c exta.c big.c lib.c app.c divp.c rt.c
Harnesses:   run.py (via arm-none-eabi-ld+libgcc), run_asarm.py (as_arm flat),
             run_ld.py (as_arm -o + ld_arm, fully self-hosted)
